menu "USB Ethernet (usb_dev_ethernet)"

    choice USBNET_CLASS
        prompt "USB Ethernet device class (settings default)"
        default USBNET_CLASS_NCM
        help
            The DEFAULT for the usb_dev_ethernet `class` setting — since
            2026-08-25 the class is selected at runtime (both compile in;
            a WiCAN host in usb_rndis mode flips the setting remotely via
            PUT /api/settings/usb_dev_ethernet).

            CDC-NCM is the class Windows ships an in-box driver for
            (UsbNcm.sys — Windows 11 24H2 removed the legacy RNDIS
            driver); macOS/Linux support it natively. The device class
            implementation is WiCAN-authored (vendored
            components/cherryusb fork; upstream CherryUSB has none).

            RNDIS remains for old Windows 10 hosts. (CDC-ECM was dropped
            with the runtime selection — Windows has NO in-box ECM
            driver, bench-verified on Win11 26200.)

        config USBNET_CLASS_NCM
            bool "CDC-NCM (Windows 11 / macOS / Linux in-box)"

        config USBNET_CLASS_RNDIS
            bool "RNDIS (legacy Windows 10; removed in Windows 11 24H2)"

    endchoice

endmenu
